  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find lines: value -> (orientation, index)\n    # orientation: 'h' for horizontal (row), 'v' for vertical (col)\n    lines = {}\n    is_line_cell = [[False for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Check rows (horizontal lines)\n    for r in range(rows):\n        first_val = grid[r][0]\n        if first_val != 0:\n            is_line = True\n            for c in range(1, cols):\n                if grid[r][c] != first_val:\n                    is_line = False\n                    break\n            if is_line:\n                lines[first_val] = ('h', r)\n                for c in range(cols):\n                    is_line_cell[r][c] = True\n    \n    # Check columns (vertical lines)\n    for c in range(cols):\n        first_val = grid[0][c]\n        if first_val != 0:\n            is_line = True\n            for r in range(1, rows):\n                if grid[r][c] != first_val:\n                    is_line = False\n                    break\n            if is_line:\n                lines[first_val] = ('v', c)\n                for r in range(rows):\n                    is_line_cell[r][c] = True\n    \n    # Initialize output with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Copy lines to output\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if is_line_cell[r][c]:\n                output[r][c] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    # Process scattered points\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if is_line_cell[r][c]:\n                continue\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val == 0:\n                continue\n            if val in lines:\n                orientation, idx = lines[val]\n                if orientation == 'h':\n                    # Project to row immediately above or below the line\n                    if r < idx and idx > 0:\n                        output[idx-1][c] = val\n                    elif r > idx and idx < rows - 1:\n                        output[idx+1][c] = val\n                else:  # 'v'\n                    # Project to column immediately left or right of the line\n                    if c < idx and idx > 0:\n                        output[r][idx-1] = val\n                    elif c > idx and idx < cols - 1:\n                        output[r][idx+1] = val\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find lines: value -> (orientation, index)\n    # orientation: 'h' for horizontal (row), 'v' for vertical (col)\n    lines = {}\n    is_line_cell = [[False for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Check rows (horizontal lines)\n    for r in range(rows):\n        first_val = grid[r][0]\n        if first_val != 0:\n            is_line = True\n            for c in range(1, cols):\n                if grid[r][c] != first_val:\n                    is_line = False\n                    break\n            if is_line:\n                lines[first_val] = ('h', r)\n                for c in range(cols):\n                    is_line_cell[r][c] = True\n    \n    # Check columns (vertical lines)\n    for c in range(cols):\n        first_val = grid[0][c]\n        if first_val != 0:\n            is_line = True\n            for r in range(1, rows):\n                if grid[r][c] != first_val:\n                    is_line = False\n                    break\n            if is_line:\n                lines[first_val] = ('v', c)\n                for r in range(rows):\n                    is_line_cell[r][c] = True\n    \n    # Initialize output with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Copy lines to output\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if is_line_cell[r][c]:\n                output[r][c] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    # Process scattered points\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if is_line_cell[r][c]:\n                continue\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val == 0:\n                continue\n            if val in lines:\n                orientation, idx = lines[val]\n                if orientation == 'h':\n                    # Project to row immediately above or below the line\n                    if r < idx and idx > 0:\n                        output[idx-1][c] = val\n                    elif r > idx and idx < rows - 1:\n                        output[idx+1][c] = val\n                else:  # 'v'\n                    # Project to column immediately left or right of the line\n                    if c < idx and idx > 0:\n                        output[r][idx-1] = val\n                    elif c > idx and idx < cols - 1:\n                        output[r][idx+1] = val\n    \n    return output",
